# U2 (review, owner 2026-11-14): the 1983 source's CHGPTR and SCNPT2 take the line from LINGT3's DX, read before CHRGTR goes past the constant, but MAKPTR's CONCHG writes the new constant at CONTXT, past the last constant CHRGTR read: after "GOTO 30 &H28" that is the &H28's three bytes. So line 30, found, becomes "GOTO 30 120" (the pointer over &H28), and "GOTO 30 &H28 &H28" becomes "GOTO 30 110 110" (the pointer over the first &H28, then SCNPT2's line number over the second). PC-BASIC changes the 30 itself. A missing line 30 is "Undefined line 30 in 10" in both.
Ok
10 GOTO 30 &H28
20 END
30 PRINT "x"
RENUM 100
Ok
LIST
100 GOTO 30 120
110 END
120 PRINT "x"
Ok
